From: Peios Packaging <packages@peios.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] posix: honor unsupported status for glob tilde mtrace companion

The tst-glob-tilde test selects the passwd database programmatically and is
therefore unsupported by Peios's fixed authority NSS policy.  Its derived
mtrace check lives in tests-special, which Rules does not filter through
tests-unsupported, and its local recipe is defined after Rules's generic
unsupported recipe.  The companion consequently runs without a trace file and
fails even when both tests are explicitly marked unsupported.

Filter this one derived target when it is named in tests-unsupported.  This
changes only the upstream test harness; no installed object is affected.
---
 posix/Makefile | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/posix/Makefile b/posix/Makefile
index 18f950f980..d6b3232852 100644
--- a/posix/Makefile
+++ b/posix/Makefile
@@ -507,6 +507,11 @@ tests-special += \
 endif
 endif
 endif
+# tests-special is not filtered by Rules's tests-unsupported handling.  Keep
+# the derived mtrace companion aligned with an explicit policy exclusion.
+ifneq ($(filter tst-glob-tilde-mem,$(tests-unsupported)),)
+tests-special := $(filter-out $(objpfx)tst-glob-tilde-mem.out,$(tests-special))
+endif
 
 include ../Rules
 
-- 
2.51.0
